# JSONPlaceholder fakes a blog API. Writes are accepted but not stored.

### List posts
GET {{placeholder}}/posts?_limit={{limit}}

> assert status == 200
> assert body.length == limit
> set postId = body[0].id

### Get a post
@needs listPosts
GET {{placeholder}}/posts/{{postId}}

> assert status == 200
> assert body.id == postId

### Comments
@needs listPosts
GET {{placeholder}}/posts/{{postId}}/comments

> assert body.length > 0
> assert body[0].email contains "@"

### Create a post
POST {{placeholder}}/posts
Content-Type: application/json; charset=utf-8

{
  "title": "{{fake.word}} and {{fake.word}}",
  "body": "Written by {{fake.name}}",
  "userId": {{randomInt(1, 10)}}
}

> assert status == 201
> assert body.id == 101

### Update a post
PATCH {{placeholder}}/posts/1

{ "title": "Edited at {{now()}}" }

> assert status == 200
> assert body.title contains "Edited"

### Delete a post
DELETE {{placeholder}}/posts/1

> assert status == 200
